  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two different deployments",
      "items": [
        "User controllers run native agents and need persistent workspace/history. The maintainer auth service runs no agent.",
        "Auth-service scale-to-zero does not mean an active conversation controller should scale to zero."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What has actually been bootstrapped",
      "items": [
        "The main-branch auth workflow verifies OIDC login and an outputs-only Bicep deployment.",
        "The selected resource group and deployment identity exist according to the runbook. No auth Container App/store/endpoint exists at this snapshot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Installer setup and teardown",
      "items": [
        "Issue #39/#53: both install scripts create the user-named GitHub Environment and user-named approval variable through host GitHub authority.",
        "Revoke works without the lost device secret. Uninstall revokes and removes the selected runtime while preserving data and shared GitHub settings. #43/#47 retain the separate auth-service delivery/resource scope."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Before user Azure apply",
      "items": [
        "Prove real storage/locking (#37), broker readiness and outstanding-token fencing (#34).",
        "Updates stop old owners before starting replacements. Runtime secrets arrive after image build; publish and runtime pull identities are separate."
      ]
    }
  ]
